  "final_answer_preview": "Under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, if a woman is raped by one or more persons acting in furtherance of a common intention, the punishment is rigorous imprisonment for a term not less than twenty years, which may extend to life imprisonment (Section 70(1)). If the victim is under eighteen years of age, the punishment is life imprisonment or death (Section 70(2)). Additionally, if the victim is under twelve years of age, the punishment is also life imprisonment or death (Section 65(2)).",
